    "customfield_12313320": "<div style='font-weight:bold;color:red;text-align:center'>This project has a <a href=\"https://lucene.apache.org/core/discussion.html\">user mailing list and an IRC channel</a> for support. If you are looking for support, or if you are not sure whether the behavior that you are observing is expected or not, please discuss it there first.</div>",
    "customfield_12314134": null,
    "duedate": null,
    "customfield_12314132": null,
    "customfield_12314131": null,
    "comment": {
      "comments": [
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12544403/comment/13218077",
          "id": "13218077",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=romseygeek",
            "name": "romseygeek",
            "key": "romseygeek",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Alan Woodward",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "body": "Trivial fix - we just check if the passed in fieldname is null, and if it is, return null.",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=romseygeek",
            "name": "romseygeek",
            "key": "romseygeek",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Alan Woodward",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "created": "2012-02-28T11:32:38.027+0000",
          "updated": "2012-02-28T11:32:38.027+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12544403/comment/13218171",
          "id": "13218171",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=mikemccand",
            "name": "mikemccand",
            "key": "mikemccand",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Michael McCandless",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "body": "Hmm I don't think the Fields.terms API should be expected to accept null (eg I don't know if the other codecs will NPE).\n\nI'd rather fix span queries to not pass the null field.  Is this happening in SpanTermQuery.getSpans()?",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=mikemccand",
            "name": "mikemccand",
            "key": "mikemccand",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Michael McCandless",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "created": "2012-02-28T13:41:17.877+0000",
          "updated": "2012-02-28T13:41:17.877+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12544403/comment/13218222",
          "id": "13218222",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=romseygeek",
            "name": "romseygeek",
            "key": "romseygeek",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Alan Woodward",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "body": "Here's a test case.  The error is thrown in SpanQuery.createWeight() when it's called on a bare SpanMultiTermQueryWrapper.\n\nIt looks as though a simple workaround is to always wrap SpanMultiTermQueryWrapper in a SpanOrQuery.  \n\nMaybe SpanOrQuery should not have a default constructor, but should require a fieldname if no clauses are supplied?",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=romseygeek",
            "name": "romseygeek",
            "key": "romseygeek",
